## Checking the Splits

The splits are given in order, as `train=`, `valid=`, and `test=` (or as a dictionary of splits by
name, with `splits=`). We'll say which column identifies a ticket (its text) and which has the
labels, and ask for rows that are nearly the same as well as rows that are the same.

::: {#c565ae99 .cell execution_count=3}
``` {.python .cell-code}
check = pb.check_splits(
    train=train, valid=valid, test=test, columns="text", label="topic", near=True
)

check.get_tabular_report()
```

