## Contamination by Other Data

`check_splits()` checks a dataset's own splits. To check that training data doesn't contain the
questions of a benchmark that the model will be judged on (or any other text that shouldn't be in
it), use the `rows_not_contaminated()` validation method, which is a step of a validation like any
other (see the [Checking Text Data](../advanced-validation/text-checks.qmd) article).

## Conclusion

A model's score on a test split is only as good as the split. The `check_splits()` function finds
the rows that leak between splits (exactly or nearly the same), the labels that a split is missing
or that only it has, and the columns whose distribution changes between splits, with a report of
each check and the issues found as messages.
